# ============================================================
#  gitignore.example — What the .gitignore SHOULD contain
#  but intentionally does NOT in the vulnerable application.
#
#  VULN-GIT-01: .env committed (secrets in version control)
#  VULN-GIT-02: *.db committed (PII in version control)
#  VULN-GIT-03: Private keys not excluded
#  VULN-GIT-04: node_modules present (forces use of old, pinned deps)
# ============================================================

# These should be ignored but are intentionally omitted in vul-app-01:
# .env
# *.db
# db/*.db
# *.pem
# *.key
# *.p12
# uploads/
# node_modules/

# Only these are "forgotten" to be ignored:
dist/
build/
coverage/
